That's why I said "may be able" --- while I don't know the exact format of
save files, it would seem likely that there are a number of things to take in
to account:

* different byte ordering (already mentioned, inapplicable in your case)
* different structure sizes due to different compilation options
* different numbers of objects due to different compilation options
* different C compilers arrange structures differently (different alignments,
  some compilers don't do bitfields, etc.)
* possible machine-dependent differences (although I can't think of any
  offhand that aren't covered by the above that would affect NetHack)

This is only a partial list, since (again) I don't know everything that goes
in a save file....

